#: ../../source/docs/aborting-autolanding.rst:5
#: f53dbfc5c4fb4231bad18f5203a315c9
msgid "How to Abort an Autolanding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/aborting-autolanding.rst:6
#: 4a792523452b4af4accf0d367613c59b
msgid "A landing-abort mechanism is provided to allow you to abort a autolanding sequence in a safe, controlled, and expected way. Custom abort behaviour can be pre-programmed as part of the mission or you can use the default abort mechanism. To enable autolanding abort feature, set param :ref:`LAND_ABORT_THR<LAND_ABORT_THR>` = 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/aborting-autolanding.rst:8
#: ccfc838c436b4ac79258d5b0cd3ff3f2
msgid "There are three aspects of this feature:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/aborting-autolanding.rst:10
#: df8331a35b7342dba3ff5ff2728dec4d
msgid ":ref:`Triggering an abort <trigger_an_abort>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/aborting-autolanding.rst:11
#: a582b4809e374791b7f7725a14ae1c17
msgid ":ref:`The behavior during the abort <behavior_during_the_abort>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/aborting-autolanding.rst:12
#: 78c4a86c97cf42d18ba8ea76ef77001c
msgid ":ref:`The mission state after the abort completes <mission_state_after_an_aborted_landing_completes>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/aborting-autolanding.rst:18
#: 64952ccf02a44430a28dc6b1340f59ef
msgid "Step 1) Abort land triggers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/aborting-autolanding.rst:19
#: e9f54c245938436e8d75044c6df71271
msgid "The are three ways to trigger an auto-landing abort. All of them will only work while in AUTO mode and currently executing a ``NAV_LAND`` waypoint mission item:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/aborting-autolanding.rst:21
#: 6e320db294e64164af750acc99a6b847
msgid "**Send the ``MAV_CMD_DO_GO_AROUND`` command using a GCS.** Mission Planner has a button labeled \"Abort Landing\" on the FlightData Actions tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/aborting-autolanding.rst:22
#: 4a3d87befae440d3a600d5c92c9574f5
msgid "**RC input Throttle > 90%**. This will trigger an abort while staying in AUTO mode. The throttle only needs to be high briefly to trigger it. Don't forget to lower it!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/aborting-autolanding.rst:23
#: cbf3edf75b57418286d2f319dcae30fb
msgid "**Mode change**. For human piloted landing abort you can switch out of AUTO mode into, for example MANUAL/STABILIZE/FBWA, and navigate the aircraft safely however you'd like. Using this method will skip abort behavior step 2 because it is being done manually. When switching back to AUTO the mission will resume as described in step 3 below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/aborting-autolanding.rst:28
#: 1ceea4b6479f4575a6d1a7764f4d856c
msgid "Step 2) Abort land flight behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/aborting-autolanding.rst:29
#: 4412c44a888544be8437b29e3c2c51c7
msgid "The abort behaviour has a default configuration and does not require a pre-planned mission. The default abort behavior is to simulate an auto-takeoff: pitch up at least 10 degrees and set throttle to :ref:`TKOFF_THR_MAX<TKOFF_THR_MAX>` and hold the heading until it reaches a target altitude of 30m. It is possible to override the pitch and altitude to allow for a customized behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/aborting-autolanding.rst:31
#: 1559767691f54545a5161338a30355de
msgid "Pitch minimum. If there was a NAV_TAKEOFF ever executed on this mission then the same minimum pitch (param1) will be reused here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/aborting-autolanding.rst:32
#: db5f1d4b912b4999a8e96cc5a1cd7fa3
msgid "Target altitude. If NAV_LAND param1 is >0 then it is used as a target altitude in meters. Else If a NAV_TAKEOFF was ever executed on this mission then the same altitude (param7) will be reused here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/aborting-autolanding.rst:34
#: 19e6fba5c1ab4b988307208af9f2edcf
msgid "This step is skipped if the abort trigger is via mode change because it is assumed the pilot manually took over and flew the aircraft to a safe altitude at the pitch and throttle of their choosing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/aborting-autolanding.rst:39
#: d99dd6b706ec411da16622a9451655ac
msgid "Step 3) Mission state after an aborted landing completes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/aborting-autolanding.rst:40
#: 1c5dad254bdc42349fdd12c58e0ddea3
msgid "Once an abort land has completed, by either reaching the target altitude or switching back to AUTO, the mission index will have changed and you will no longer be executing a NAV_LAND command. The mission index will change to be one of these three options and checked for in this order:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/aborting-autolanding.rst:42
#: 7776a904d1f148dd83cc986763fa3698
msgid "If the NAV_LAND mission item is followed by mission item :ref:`CONTINUE_AND_CHANGE_ALT <mav_cmd_nav_continue_and_change_alt>` with param1 = 0 or 1 then the mission index will increment once to that command and execute it like normal. This can be followed by further post-abort mission planning for any custom planned mission behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/aborting-autolanding.rst:43
#: ecd0b73eb9a845fb9046410217aef11b
msgid "Else If there is a :ref:`DO_LAND_START <mav_cmd_do_land_start>` in the mission then it jumps to that index."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/aborting-autolanding.rst:44
#: a2f59ed08f3a4511ac527d541dce4cae
msgid "Else the mission index decrements once to be the index before the NAV_LAND. This will ensure the same landing approach is repeated."
msgstr ""
